136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Youth unemployment is a major socio-economic issue in Sri Lanka, especially in a period of economic uncertainty and changes in the labour market. High levels of unemployment among young people can lead to long-term income problems, loss of skills, and social challenges. Therefore, understanding the patterns and factors related to youth unemployment is important for informed decision-making.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (This study examines youth unemployment patterns in Sri Lanka using data from the Sri Lanka Labour Force Survey \(LFS\) 2023. The analysis focuses on how unemployment varies across key demographic, educational, and geographic characteristics of the youth population.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (The main aim of this study is to provide a clear understanding of youth unemployment in Sri Lanka and to identify the key factors associated with unemployment among youth.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
